    "llm_raw_response": "<response>\n  <verdict>Existing</verdict>\n  <justification>Whole-exome sequencing in a human cohort of ID/ASD patients identified a pathogenic ACTB variant among genes already known to be associated with ID/ASD (PMID 34948243), providing direct human genetic evidence of contribution to the ASD/ID phenotype. ACTB loss-of-function mutations are established as causing a pleiotropic developmental disorder with intellectual disability (PMID 29220674), and gain-of-function missense mutations cause Baraitser-Winter syndrome featuring intellectual disability (PMID 27625340). A 7p22.1 microduplication including ACTB was detected in a child diagnosed with autism, with ACTB proposed as a candidate gene (PMID 25893121). While ACTB is firmly linked to neurodevelopmental disorders and intellectual disability, the evidence specifically for autism causation is limited rather than definitively replicated, supporting an \"Existing\" classification.</justification>\n  <pmids>\n    <pmid>34948243</pmid>\n    <pmid>29220674</pmid>\n    <pmid>27625340</pmid>\n    <pmid>25893121</pmid>\n  </pmids>\n</response>",
